				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$32 \times 1024$$\end{document}.Fig. 1
The general process of feature extraction

ESM-2 [39] is a language model based on Transformer that uses attention mechanisms to learn the interaction patterns between paired amino acids in input sequences. It is also the most high-performance language model developed to date for proteins. Compared to the previous ESM-1b, it not only improves the training parameters and model structure but also increases computational data and resources. On the benchmark of structural prediction, ESM-2 also surpasses other protein language models. Similar to the ProtT5 model, the embedding layer of ESM-2 converts the input amino acid sequence into a high-dimensional vector representation, including words, sentence pairs, and word position information, and optimizes it for protein sequences. By stacking multiple Transformer blocks to capture long-term dependencies in the sequence, a deep representation of the sequence is generated, and a numerical matrix of \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
