The second way is to process it into feature information through the Transformer encoder [43]. The use of Transformer encoders to process peptide sequence information utilizes a multi-layered model structure. The Transformer model includes multiple encoder and decoder parts, which can be split, making it convenient for us to change the structure of the model as needed. Since the Transformer does not contain a looping part, the security dependency attention mechanism is used to depict global dependencies. Therefore, positional encoding [43] is also required when using the Transformer encoder. The use of absolute positional encoding can integrate positional information into the input of the Transformer, which is achieved by adding the word embedding vector and the word position embedding vector. The formula is as follows:3\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
