In the experiment, convolutional neural networks were used to extract local features of peptide sequences, and different convolutional kernel sizes can extract different local information. As mentioned in the feature section, the sizes of these five types of feature information are not the same. Therefore, to fully utilize their respective features, we used convolutional neural networks for each input information. When other parameters are the same, the size of the convolutional kernel may not be completely the same. For example, the feature information obtained through the Transformer encoder is suitable for using a convolutional layer of size 2, while the feature information encoded through one-hot is suitable for using a convolutional layer of size 5. Through convolutional layers, the output shape of features becomes the same, all of which are (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
