				\begin{document}$$b_{s}$$\end{document}, 32, 64), where 64 is the number of filters.

To prevent overfitting issues, we used a max pooling layer and a dropout layer after each convolutional layer to compress the amount of data and parameters. These two layers do not change the shape of the input. Therefore, the output shapes of these two layers are (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
