Next is the bidirectional long short-term memory network(Bi-LSTM) layer, which consists of two LSTMs [44] in opposite directions. LSTM is an improved recurrent neural network (RNN) [45] that solves the problems of vanishing and exploding gradients when using recurrent neural networks to process sequences, while also learning long-term dependency information. It includes mechanisms such as forget gates, output gates, and input gates, which are defined as follows:7\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
